{%- comment -%}
  Evidence-led Shettles Method resource page.
  PDF source files are bundled with the theme so visitors can open the originals.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section
  class="sm-page"
  style="--sm-bg: {{ section.settings.background }}; --sm-surface: {{ section.settings.surface }}; --sm-ink: {{ section.settings.text_color }}; --sm-accent: {{ section.settings.accent }}; --sm-space: {{ section.settings.section_spacing }}px;"
>
  <header class="sm-hero">
    <div class="sm-shell sm-hero__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="sm-kicker">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        <h1>{{ section.settings.hero_title }}</h1>
        <p class="sm-lede">{{ section.settings.hero_text }}</p>
        <div class="sm-actions" aria-label="Page navigation">
          <a class="sm-button sm-button--primary" href="#research">{{ section.settings.research_cta }}</a>
          <a class="sm-button sm-button--secondary" href="#publications">{{ section.settings.publications_cta }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="sm-notice" aria-label="Important evidence notice">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 2.8 20h18.4L12 3Z"/><path d="M12 9v5M12 17.2v.1"/></svg>
        <div>
          <strong>Important to know</strong>
          <p>{{ section.settings.disclaimer }}</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="sm-shell sm-choices" aria-label="Explore this page">
    <a class="sm-choice" href="#research">
      <span class="sm-choice__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><circle cx="16" cy="15" r="6"/><path d="M5 36c1-8 5-12 11-12s10 4 11 12M32 7v13l-7 13h18l-7-13V7M29 13h10"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span><strong>Research</strong><small>Understand the theory, later findings and current evidence position.</small></span>
      <span class="sm-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span>
    </a>
    <a class="sm-choice" href="#publications">
      <span class="sm-choice__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="M10 5h21l7 7v31H10zM31 5v9h7M17 22h14M17 29h14M17 36h9"/><path d="m34 32 8-8 3 3-8 8-5 2z"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span><strong>Publications</strong><small>Open the supplied papers and review verified academic sources.</small></span>
      <span class="sm-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span>
    </a>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <section class="sm-section sm-intro" aria-labelledby="sm-intro-title">
      <div class="sm-shell sm-reading">
        <p class="sm-kicker">Overview</p>
        <h2 id="sm-intro-title">What is the Shettles Method?</h2>
        <p>The Shettles Method became popular as a natural, preconception approach to sex selection. It proposes that timing intercourse in relation to ovulation, supposed differences between X-bearing and Y-bearing sperm, and conditions in the vaginal environment could influence chromosomal sex.</p>
        <p>These ideas are historical claims and hypotheses, not established medical facts. Later research has disputed whether intercourse timing can be used reliably in practice. Anyone seeking individual fertility or reproductive-health advice should consult an appropriately qualified healthcare professional.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="research" class="sm-section sm-section--tint" aria-labelledby="research-title">
      <div class="sm-shell">
        <div class="sm-heading">
          <p class="sm-kicker">Research</p>
          <h2 id="research-title">Claims, context and evidence</h2>
          <p>Plain-language summaries designed to keep the original theory separate from what studies have actually established.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sm-research-grid">
          <article class="sm-panel">
            <span class="sm-number">01</span>
            <h3>The original theory</h3>
            <p>Historically, intercourse closer to ovulation was claimed to favour Y-bearing sperm, while intercourse several days beforehand was claimed to favour X-bearing sperm. Popular versions also described differences in sperm speed, durability, size and behaviour, and sometimes included vaginal pH or particular sexual practices.</p>
            <p class="sm-callout">These are historical claims, not established medical facts.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="sm-panel">
            <span class="sm-number">02</span>
            <h3>What later studies found</h3>
            <p>A 1985 study of a modified technique found no statistically significant difference from uncontrolled intercourse. A 1991 meta-analysis did not support timing intercourse as a practical, reliable sex-selection method.</p>
            <p><a href="#pub-simcock">Read the 1985 source</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&#183;</span> <a href="#pub-gray">Read the 1991 source</a></p>
          </article>
          <article class="sm-panel">
            <span class="sm-number">03</span>
            <h3>Current evidence position</h3>
            <p>Current published evidence does not establish that intercourse timing, sexual position, vaginal pH manipulation, or other popular Shettles recommendations can reliably determine the sex of a baby.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="sm-panel">
            <span class="sm-number">04</span>
            <h3>Safety and medical guidance</h3>
            <p>The method should not replace professional fertility advice. Avoid unsafe vaginal pH manipulation, douching, restrictive diets or unverified supplements. Discuss fertility, pregnancy and reproductive-health questions with a qualified healthcare professional.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="sm-library" aria-labelledby="research-library-title">
          <div class="sm-heading sm-heading--compact">
            <p class="sm-kicker">PDF library</p>
            <h3 id="research-library-title">Research summaries</h3>
            <p>Internal Genesyx reference material. These documents are explanatory summaries, not peer-reviewed publications.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-card-grid sm-card-grid--two">
            <article class="sm-pdf-card">
              <span class="sm-tag">Internal overview · 3 pages</span>
              <h4>Shettles Method: Research Overview</h4>
              <p>Study notes covering timing, diet and laboratory research, with methods, sample sizes and limitations kept attached to individual findings.</p>
              <div class="sm-link-group">
                <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--primary" href="{{ 'Shettles_Method_Research_Overview.pdf' | asset_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read full PDF <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="sm-pdf-card">
              <span class="sm-tag">Internal overview · 1 page</span>
              <h4>Genesyx and the Shettles Method</h4>
              <p>A concise explanation of how Genesyx organises cycle observation, timing, nutrition and pH information without claiming that the method is proven.</p>
              <div class="sm-link-group">
                <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--primary" href="{{ 'Genesyx_and_the_Shettles_Method.pdf' | asset_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read full PDF <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sm-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-summary-title">
      <div class="sm-shell">
        <div class="sm-heading">
          <p class="sm-kicker">At a glance</p>
          <h2 id="evidence-summary-title">How to read the evidence</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sm-evidence-grid">
          <article><span>Historical claim</span><h3>Timing and environment may favour one sperm type</h3><p>The theory proposes predictable differences between X-bearing and Y-bearing sperm.</p></article>
          <article><span>Research finding</span><h3>Results do not establish a reliable natural method</h3><p>Study designs and questions differ, and controlled evidence has not validated the practical claims.</p></article>
          <article><span>Practical conclusion</span><h3>Do not present the method as proven</h3><p>The Shettles Method should not be presented as proven, guaranteed, or equivalent to clinically validated reproductive technologies.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="publications" class="sm-section sm-section--dark" aria-labelledby="publications-title">
      <div class="sm-shell">
        <div class="sm-heading">
          <p class="sm-kicker">Publications</p>
          <h2 id="publications-title">Supplied academic papers</h2>
          <p>Open the full PDFs supplied for this resource. Each card states the study design so findings are not mistaken for proof of the wider Shettles Method.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm-card-grid">
          <article class="sm-pdf-card sm-pdf-card--dark">
            <span class="sm-tag">Observational cohort · 2008 · 8 pages</span>
            <h3>You are what your mother eats: evidence for maternal preconception diet influencing foetal sex in humans</h3>
            <p><strong>Fiona Mathews, Paul J. Johnson and Andrew Neil</strong><br>Proceedings of the Royal Society B · DOI 10.1098/rspb.2008.0105</p>
            <p>Observed an association between preconception diet and birth sex in 740 British women. It did not test or establish the Shettles Method as a reliable intervention.</p>
            <div class="sm-link-group">
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--light" href="{{ 'Mathews_2008_Preconception_Diet_and_Foetal_Sex.pdf' | asset_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read full PDF <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--ghost" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18430648/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubMed record <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="sm-pdf-card sm-pdf-card--dark">
            <span class="sm-tag">Laboratory study · 2017 · 9 pages</span>
            <h3>Environmental Exposure of Sperm Sex-Chromosomes: A Gender Selection Technique</h3>
            <p><strong>Ibukun P. Oyeyipo, Michelle van der Linde and Stefan S. du Plessis</strong><br>Toxicological Research · DOI 10.5487/TR.2017.33.4.315</p>
            <p>Tested 18 semen samples under different laboratory conditions. Its sperm-enrichment findings are not pregnancy outcomes and do not validate at-home pH manipulation.</p>
            <div class="sm-link-group">
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--light" href="{{ 'Oyeyipo_2017_XY_Sperm_and_Environmental_Exposure.pdf' | asset_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read full PDF <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--ghost" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29071016/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubMed record <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="sm-pdf-card sm-pdf-card--dark">
            <span class="sm-tag">Uncontrolled retrospective report · 2022 · 7 pages</span>
            <h3>Using Non-Invasive Methods to Choose Gender; Sex Selection with Diet and Determination of Ovulation Time in Iran</h3>
            <p><strong>Dariush Farhud and colleagues</strong><br>Iranian Journal of Public Health · DOI 10.18502/ijph.v51i8.10275</p>
            <p>Reported outcomes from a combined diet, timing and lifestyle programme. The uncontrolled retrospective design cannot establish that the intervention caused the reported outcomes.</p>
            <div class="sm-link-group">
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--light" href="{{ 'Farhud_2022_Diet_Ovulation_Timing_and_Sex_Selection.pdf' | asset_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read full PDF <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--ghost" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36249107/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubMed record <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="sm-verified" aria-labelledby="verified-title">
          <div class="sm-heading sm-heading--compact">
            <p class="sm-kicker">Verified sources</p>
            <h3 id="verified-title">Research directly assessing sex-selection claims</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-source-list">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'publication' -%}
                <article id="{{ block.settings.anchor }}" class="sm-source" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <div><span class="sm-tag">{{ block.settings.publication_type }} · {{ block.settings.year }}</span><h4>{{ block.settings.title }}</h4></div>
                  <dl><div><dt>Authors</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.authors }}</dd></div><div><dt>Journal</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.journal }}</dd></div><div><dt>DOI</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.doi }}</dd></div></dl>
                  <p>{{ block.settings.summary }}</p>
                  <div class="sm-source__actions">
                    <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--light" href="{{ block.settings.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubMed record <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
                    <a class="sm-link-button sm-link-button--ghost" href="https://doi.org/{{ block.settings.doi | strip | escape }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open DOI <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
                  </div>
                </article>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sm-section sm-section--tint" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="sm-shell sm-faq-layout">
        <div class="sm-heading sm-heading--sticky"><p class="sm-kicker">Questions</p><h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2><p>Short answers based on the current evidence position.</p></div>
        <div class="sm-faq">
          {% assign questions = "What is the Shettles Method?|Does the Shettles Method work?|Can timing intercourse determine the sex of a baby?|Is the Shettles Method scientifically proven?|Can vaginal pH determine the sex of a baby?|Is the Shettles Method safe?|What should someone do if they have fertility concerns?" | split: "|" %}
          {% assign answers = "It is a historical natural sex-selection method based mainly on timing intercourse around ovulation and proposed differences between X-bearing and Y-bearing sperm.|Published evidence does not establish it as a reliable way to determine a baby's sex, so it should not be presented as proven or guaranteed.|No reliable practical method has been established using intercourse timing alone.|No. Some studies explore related biological or observational questions, but the complete method has not been scientifically validated as reliable.|Laboratory conditions can affect sperm, but that does not show that manipulating vaginal pH at home can reliably determine a baby's sex. Douching or unsafe pH manipulation should be avoided.|Tracking a cycle is generally low risk, but restrictive diets, unverified supplements, douching and vaginal pH manipulation may be unsafe. Seek individual medical advice.|Speak with an appropriately qualified healthcare professional or fertility specialist for assessment and personal guidance." | split: "|" %}
          {%- for question in questions -%}<details><summary>{{ question }}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{{ answers[forloop.index0] }}</p></details>{%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="sm-footer"><div class="sm-shell"><strong>Medical disclaimer</strong><p>{{ section.settings.footer_disclaimer }}</p></div></footer>
</section>

<style>
